  "verification": [
    "Three real Hall lessons render both optional bridges before their original formulas; native open state, local answers, original exercise steps and editable drafts survive ordinary tabs.",
    "Independent Bargmann/projector and QWZ small-loop checks, gauge choices, orientation and occupation/entropy examples test the stated conventions.",
    "All 735 current-stage requirements retain their values and strict tolerances; all differences receive human labels, values and comparison explanations.",
    "77 real project-stage form roundtrips cover 32 action adapters; standard workbench analyze snapshots cover the remaining action and all 230 database groups.",
    "Real application routing tests preserve the chosen project instance, stage and notes; input loading waits for explicit computation, consumes the original snapshot, and isolates fresh external navigation.",
    "The app, projects, comparison tool and topic views use one canonical calculation-notebook module instance, including app-only analyze captures."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "These are interface, input-roundtrip and mathematical-reference checks, not measured student learning outcomes or a complete audit of all curricula.",
    "A finite loop estimates local curvature; it does not compute a full Brillouin-zone Chern number or transport coefficient.",
    "The zero-temperature threshold half-occupation convention and zero transport entropy kernel are stated separately.",
    "Input restoration covers registered GUI fields and options with an explicit 4 MB editable input bound; unsupported API-only settings or custom workbench operations/bases are rejected. Existing saved records remain unchanged.",
    "The teaching_labs project adapter covers the currently used Lie su2_coupling subtype; future teaching subtypes need their own verified adapters."
  ],
